## Fault Detection and Recovery

All values below come from our test runs.

| Metric | Observed |
|---|---|
| Crash and deadlock detection time | 300 to 400 ms after the last good heartbeat |
| Overrun detection time | about 530 ms (3 overrun cycles of 150 ms each) |
| Process restart duration | 1 to 3 ms |
| Downtime, from last good beat to first heartbeat of the new process | about 495 to 740 ms |
| Recovery order in a dual fault | Brakes, then Engine, then Infotainment |
| Effect on unaffected ECUs | None, their heartbeats continued without a gap |

Detection time varies between 300 and 400 ms because the watchdog checks on a 100 ms tick.

### Scenarios tested

| Scenario | Command | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Single crash | `1`, `2`, `3` | Detected, restarted and recovered automatically |
| Dual fault | `4` | All three recovered in priority order |
| Deadlock | `h1`, `h2` | Heartbeat stopped, fault detected, ECU restarted |
| Overrun | `o1`, `o2` | Three overruns counted, fault raised, ECU restarted |
| Clean shutdown | `q` | Supervisor and ECUs stop cleanly |

