## How to Reproduce the Profiler Trace

1. Start the supervisor on the Pi and wait until all three ECUs show **HEALTHY**.
2. In Momentics, switch to the **QNX System Profiler** perspective.
3. Choose **Log** with **Kernel Log of** your target, set the save location and click **Log**.
4. Click inside the supervisor console and inject faults (`1`, `4`, `o2`), a few seconds apart.
5. Stop the kernel logging session. Momentics then opens the `.kev` trace file.
6. Use the **Summary**, **CPU Usage** and **Timeline** views to take the screenshots above.

> The Pi must run the instrumented kernel (`procnto-smp-instr`) for kernel logging to work.